(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector)), (:adr/note "This is a PROPOSAL, not an accepted decision. No implementation work has started. Requires owner review before status can change to accepted."), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/proposal-summary "{:problem \"aiueos's device-access quartet (pci-config/dma-map/irq-subscribe/mmio-map) are deterministic stubs -- real hardware access remains unimplemented, per ADR-2607022900's closing summary\", :root-cause \"NOT a Rust-vs-Java question (corrected in ADR-2607022900 follow-up 2) -- no unprivileged userspace process in ANY language can do raw MMIO/DMA without root+/dev/mem or KVM/hypervisor privilege or being the kernel itself (confirmed via Solo5's own hvt/spt architecture: the TENDER holds privilege, the GUEST never touches raw MMIO)\", :proposed-design {:pattern \"separate minimal-privilege 'device-access provider' subprocess, same EDN-over-stdio pattern as aiueos.decide (ADR-2607022700 precedent)\", :privilege-scope \"ONLY the device-access provider process holds elevated privilege (root/CAP_SYS_RAWIO or equivalent) -- the JVM tender/broker/CLJC decision layer stays unprivileged, minimizing attack surface\", :invariant-preserved \"the device-access provider still never judges capability itself -- aiueos.execute only forwards a request AFTER the broker has already granted it (ADR-2607022700's core invariant carried forward)\", :implementation-language-recommendation \"Java 22+ java.lang.foreign (Foreign Function & Memory API) as first choice, NOT Rust -- keeps consistency with ADR-2607022900's Chicory/JVM direction, but requires a JDK 21->22+ bump (out of scope for this ADR); Rust remains a documented alternative if the owner decides the privileged-process boundary is worth reintroducing Rust for\"}, :staged-plan [\"spike a minimal KVM-based VMM (single PCI device MMIO read/write) in Java 22+ FFM to validate real hardware access is achievable\" \"design the device-access provider's EDN-over-stdio protocol, mirroring aiueos.decide's request/response shape\" \"replace aiueos.execute's device-access-stub internals with real provider calls, keeping the stub function signatures unchanged to minimize impact on the existing 186-test suite\" \"select and document a privilege-grant mechanism (setuid/capabilities/dedicated service account) for deployment\"], :open-decisions-for-owner [\"approve/reject this design direction (status proposed -> accepted/rejected)\" \"JDK 21->22+ bump acceptability (CI + all .clj/.cljc dependents impact, out of scope here)\" \"Rust reintroduction for the minimal privileged provider process only -- tradeoff against ADR-2607022900's completed Rust-dependency elimination\"]}"), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "aiueos-privileged-device-access-tender-design"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607022900-aiueos-chicory-jvm-native-adapter" "adr-2607022700-aiueos-native-adapter-tender-design" "adr-2607022400-kototama-unikernel-tender-runtime-vocabulary")), (:adr/status "proposed"), (:adr/id "adr-2607030900-aiueos-privileged-device-access-tender-design"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-03"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607030900: aiueos の生ハードウェアアクセス（device-access quartet: pci-config/dma-map/irq-subscribe/mmio-map）を実現する特権/hypervisor 協調レイヤーの設計提案\n\n**Status**: proposed（未承認——実装前にオーナーレビュー必須）\n**Date**: 2026-07-03\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2607022900 は aiueos の native adapter 実行層と CLI 本体を Rust から\nJVM/Clojure + Chicory へ完全移行した。残る恒久的ギャップの1つ、生ハード\nウェアアクセス（device-access quartet）は現在も未着手——`aiueos.execute`\nでは常に`0`を返すdeterministic stub。\n\nADR-2607022900 follow-up 2 で判明した通り、これは「Rust か Java か」の\n問題ではなく「特権/hypervisor協調レイヤーの不在」という言語非依存の問題。\nSolo5のhvt/sptアーキテクチャ調査により、非特権プロセスはどの言語でも\n生MMIO/DMAに触れないことを確認済み。\n\n## Decision（提案）\n\n1. **特権昇格の範囲を最小化**: ADR-2607022700のdecision subprocessパターン\n   と同じ形で、別プロセス（device-access provider）にのみ特権を持たせ、\n   JVM tender/broker/CLJC判定層は非特権のまま保つ。\n2. **実装言語はJava 22+ FFMを第一候補**（Rustではなく）——ただしJDK 21→22+\n   バンプが前提、CIへの影響調査が必要。\n3. **段階的実装**: KVMベース最小VMMのspike → provider プロトコル設計 →\n   device-access-stub の内部実装差し替え → 権限付与方式の選定。\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) 攻撃対象領域を最小化、ADR-2607022700の不変条件を継承\n- (−) JDKバンプ前提、CI影響調査必要\n- (−) Rust再導入の代替案はADR-2607022900の成果を部分的に後退させる\n- (−) KVMベース最小VMMは大きな実装作業——本ADRは設計提案に留める\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607022700, ADR-2607022900, ADR-2607022400\n- Solo5 architecture.md/README.edn\n- JEP 454 (Java 22 Foreign Function & Memory API)"), (:adr/deciders (vector)), (:adr/date "2026-07-03"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative false), (:adr/title "ADR-2607030900: aiueos の生ハードウェアアクセス（device-access quartet）を実現する特権/hypervisor 協調レイヤーの設計提案"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))